# Redis connection

`RedisConfig` reads `spring.data.redis.host`, `port`, `username`, `password`, and `ssl.enabled`. Keys under `spring.redis.*` are ignored.

The Upstash instance uses username `default`, port `6379`, and SSL on. Keep the password in `application.properties`. Do not hardcode the host or password in `RedisConfig`.

Do not set a `<version>` on `spring-boot-starter-data-redis`. Boot 3.3.11 supplies it. Version `2.7.18` breaks startup. Leave Jedis unused. The factory is Lettuce.

The dev API on port `8095` must not use the verify harness Redis on port `6380`.

```properties
# BAD — RedisConfig never reads this prefix
spring.redis.host=fancy-lamb-246550.upstash.io
spring.redis.ssl.enabled=true

# GOOD
spring.data.redis.host=fancy-lamb-246550.upstash.io
spring.data.redis.port=6379
spring.data.redis.username=default
spring.data.redis.ssl.enabled=true
```

```xml
<!-- BAD -->
<artifactId>spring-boot-starter-data-redis</artifactId>
<version>2.7.18</version>

<!-- GOOD -->
<artifactId>spring-boot-starter-data-redis</artifactId>
```
